Z||000000||Hippocrat||09-17-2001||12:47 AM||||Some 4cyls came with 5spd tranys as did the 6cyls .. are they the same trany or no? if not are all 4cyl 5spd the same and all 6cyl 5spd the same? thanx for any clarification you guys can offer ..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||09-17-2001||02:44 AM||||No, the trannies are different from he 6 cyl and 4 cyl's in not only gear ratio but manufacturer and strength as well.<BR>The 6 cyl trannies are supposedly stronger but then again Archie has used many of the <BR>Isuzu 4 cyl trannies behind V8's with no problems so far.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||09-17-2001||10:44 AM||||Yep, There is the Isuzu and the Getrag. The getrag came with the V6 and the Isuzu with the 4's. I love the Isuzu. I have it hooked to my V6 in my 88 Coupe. I have the "Notchy getrag in my 88 GT I don't like it as much as the Isuzu.<P>Just my opinion. Most like the Getrag<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
